Here is the above pseudocode rewritten in [[Python (programming language)|Python 3]]:

<syntaxhighlight lang="python3">
from random import shuffle

def is_sorted(data) -> bool:
    """Determine whether the data is sorted."""
    return all(a <= b for a, b in zip(data, data[1:]))

def bogosort(data) -> list:
    """Shuffle data until sorted."""
    while not is_sorted(data):
        shuffle(data)
    return data
</syntaxhighlight>

This code assumes that {{code|data}} is a simple, mutable, array-like data structure—like Python's built-in {{code|list}}—whose elements can be compared without issue.

